+
+NUMERICAL R12-S check: reconstructed at q=1000033 with its defining scalar formulas (not asserted to be a binary set); it has K about 50.00055, 99.03% of modes within 10% of -K, and RMS[P-inverse-(b-1/2)] about 0.004903, yet its Boolean square identity fails. Thus saturation plus that misinterpreted flatness test can look very good on a forbidden fake. The actual squared-plateau and Boolean residuals are saved as separate metrics.
