Round 15 is complete. The full audit, proofs, failed steps, and computational record are in [tdense15_report.md](/Users/jmercedes/Desktop/Projects/Research/chowla-cosine/.research/agents/tdense15_report.md).

- **Part A — PROVED:** P66 passes the step-by-step audit. E94b was independently verified using sign-controlled squaring and Sturm’s theorem. The dedicated rational certificate proves **D_(2/3) <= 73/1000**, extending the dense exponent-1/3 theorem to every **C < 1000/73 ≈ 13.69863**, with an ineffective positive constant.
- **Part B — precise obstruction:** Derived explicit defect, spectral-core, zero-spike, and parity bounds. These expose the missing scale: excluding equality by a fixed amount improves only the constant at exponent 1/4. The report states one explicit missing estimate, WRS(eta), and proves its conditional implication to an exponent above 1/4. **No new unconditional cyclic exponent is claimed.**
- **Verification:** The independent certificate check passed 767 covering leaves, 188 support lines, and 64 continuum Schur cells. Adversarial checks covered Paley sets, stored E41/E90 sets, random-profile half-sets, and non-Boolean fakes.

The [exact certificate](/Users/jmercedes/Desktop/Projects/Research/chowla-cosine/.research/agents/tdense15_scratch/certificate_sigma.json), [independent verification](/Users/jmercedes/Desktop/Projects/Research/chowla-cosine/.research/agents/tdense15_scratch/sigma_independent.json), and reproducibility manifest are preserved in the scratch directory. All computation used the specified VM wrapper with four cores; no subagents or commits were used.
